// GG-ZERO RGB DIFFUSION ARENA — I-13 numeric semantic source witness
// Based on canonical I + twelve semantic words (I13-H1.1 / TRUNK.md).
// This file records numeric intention, not an executable all-opcode compiler output.
// The working cartridge is hand-assembled to Z80 in games/rgb-diffusion-game.js.
// 3 paired RGB channels, 2^3 color combinations, IN(-) unlit, OUT(+) lit.
I RED <- 1
I GREEN <- 2
I BLUE <- 4
I RGB_STATES <- 2 * 2 * 2
I WIDTH <- 16
I HEIGHT <- 12
I GAME_CELLS <- WIDTH * HEIGHT
I BORDER_STRIDE <- 18
I REACTOR_X <- 8
I REACTOR_Y <- 6
I REACTOR_WHITE <- RED + GREEN + BLUE
// Operational rule compiled explicitly to Z80:
// NEXT(x,y) = CURRENT(x,y) OR LEFT OR RIGHT OR NORTH OR SOUTH
// Color mixing is the binary OR of independent 1-bit channels.
// Z / Button1: deposit selected bit at the cursor.
// X / Button2: cycle selected bit 1 -> 2 -> 4 -> 1.
// Arrow keys: change cursor location. START: reset/seed a new round.
// Reactor rewards WHITE (7) only after an actual user paint action.
// This is an illustrative binary cellular automaton, not Fick's law
// and not hardware quantum diffusion.
